abstract: "An ongoing mathematical-physics research program developing a falsifiable test architecture for physical-to-experiential bridge claims. The repository formalizes deterministic and stochastic factorization tests, intervention-resolved causal structure, temporal and multiscale compatibility, finite-data certification, target-provenance non-circularity, target-measurement channel robustness, target-channel identifiability, finite-sample target-channel recovery, target-model adequacy and four-view overidentification, quantum operational sufficiency tests, adaptive experiment design, and certified calibration and optimization. Proposition 71 proves that targets constructed as functions or descriptor-only channels of the tested physical descriptor satisfy the corresponding bridge or screening-off condition by construction. Proposition 72 adds the noisy-target layer and proves one-way residual transfer, witness erasure, target-TV contraction, channel-stability bounds, and a conservative finite-sample target-separation certificate. Proposition 73 gives an explicit population inversion for a nondegenerate binary latent target observed through three conditionally independent binary views, identifies the P72 stability coefficients up to the unavoidable latent-label symmetry, and proves by construction that two views do not generally identify individual channel reliabilities. Proposition 74 propagates one simultaneous eight-cell finite-sample confidence event through the P73 inversion, adds a covariance nondegeneracy gate, and gives conservative confidence intervals for the latent target-channel quantities. Proposition 75 separates identifiability from model adequacy: it shows that three binary views are generically just-identified, while a fourth binary view creates six generic overidentifying degrees of freedom, observable covariance-tetrad and cross-triple consistency obligations, a fourth-centered-moment relation, and a full-law reconstruction audit. The downstream calibration branch includes lower-bounded heterogeneous calibration and exact primal-dual gap decomposition through P70. Current documented theorem frontier: P75. The physical-to-experiential bridge remains open, and the project does not assume that consciousness is a scalar, state of matter, quantum variable, or additional spacetime dimension."
